<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">Francisco Hernández Girón</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1510–1554</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Francisco Hernández Girón was a Spanish conquistador who in November 1553 led the last major rebellion of the encomenderos in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a>, provoked by royal measures to abolish the forced personal service of indigenous people. Starting at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cusco">Cusco</a>, his forces defeated a royal army at Chuquinga in 1554 but were routed at Pucará later that year. He was captured and executed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lima">Lima</a> in December 1554.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/francisco-hernandez-giron.jpg" alt="Francisco Hernández Girón" width="320" height="464" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Felipe Guamán Poma de Ayala · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hern%C3%A1ndez_Gir%C3%B3n.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
